  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In the dream formation fight, Black Tigress uses the move against Fang Yuan’s divination tortoise. It pierces the tortoise shell, which Fang Yuan treats as the hardest part of that body, and still injures his tough ancient desolate beast flesh despite non-conflicting dao marks. Each activation needs her to stretch out her tongue. The strike is formless rather than an obvious projectile, concentrates damage rather than sweeping a wide area, and can hit at distance.",
      "chapters": [
        1353
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lady_white_rabbit",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later listing names Black Tigress’s tiger lick killer move beside Bai Xiang and Lead Soul Into Dream.",
      "chapters": [
        1422
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_lead_soul_into_dream"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan tests sight and smell with fog and stench, and the move still lands. Heating the shell makes her cringe from heat; a salty change disgusts her. He concludes the targeting uses taste, and that each lick needs the tongue. He also reasons that Shadow Sect food path true inheritances fit a non-standard path that can hurt that defensive tortoise form. Once he counters the taste aim, she stops using this move and switches to other long range methods.",
      "chapters": [
        1353
      ],
